# 2026-09-17: 1.2.0-alpha -> 1.4.0-alpha (extractor batch, Task 12). Ancestor
#   edges now resolve by ARITY before scope rule 0: FilterCandidatesByArity
#   (new; added to the manifest) narrows the candidate set in ResolveAncestry's
#   edge loop and in ResolveTypeNameToClass.PickCandidate, and
#   NormalizeAncestorName hands back the type arguments. All of that decides
#   WHICH type_ancestors row is written, so it is DERIVED rows only, no parse
#   change: remedy is index --all --resolve-only.
#
#   ABSORBS AN UNPINNED BUMP. 1.2.0 -> 1.3.0 (bc2e39dc, 2026-09-16: member-access
#   refs bind properties/fields and accessor calls earn call_edges rows) moved
#   the constant but never re-pinned this baseline, so the active line below was
#   still 1.2.0 while the source declared 1.3.0. The guard reported "changed AND
#   bumped" on every run since -- green, but no longer pinning anything. This
#   entry pins 1.4.0 against the current surface and closes that gap.
#
#   Superseded: 1.2.0-alpha|6f0b03699c2cb23f83c8b5831a0013c92cacbea98da8759f033fd528acad2f2f

# 2026-09-17: hash re-pinned WITHIN 1.4.0-alpha (final-review wave, ruling R19:
#   no version constant moves in this wave). No index has yet been resolved
#   under 1.4.0, so the pin moves within the same version instead of bumping
#   -- there is no 1.4.0 edge anywhere for a bump to invalidate. What moved:
#   GenericArity now counts PARAMETERS, not constraint commas
#   (<T: class, constructor> = 1; <S: IUnknown; I: IUnknown> = 2), which is
#   the number FilterCandidatesByArity compares, so every edge onto a
#   constrained generic resolves differently (final review #1); the manifest
#   gained the three Core.Model helpers that decide which edge is written
#   (GenericArity, SplitGenericName, StripGenericSegments -- the last moved
#   here from the parser) and GetTransitiveAncestors (late resolution), and
#   EXCLUDEs PreferArity (query-side reader); src\index CallResolver.
#   FindChildOfKind declines on same-named locals of differing Signature.
#   The guard itself changed too: spans are cut from the implementation
#   section only (Core.Model declares free functions at column 1 in its
#   interface, which would otherwise hash the next routine's doc comment),
#   the drift vocabulary gained arity|generic, and the drift walk covers
#   Core.Model. Remedy when an index exists: index --all --resolve-only.
#
#   Superseded: 1.4.0-alpha|2cda913770535660645b65f9daceb3483b729158dbdf64d2836be374149f536c
#
# 2026-09-17: hash re-pinned WITHIN 1.4.0-alpha (batch residue; ruling R19
#   still holds -- no index has been resolved under 1.4.0 yet, the overnight
#   rebuild is the first). Commit "fix(resolve): ResolveAccessor narrows
#   overloaded accessors by arity or declines; FindSymbolsByExactName strips
#   generics per dotted segment (batch residue)". What moved: src\index
#   CallResolver.ResolveAccessor no longer first-matches an OVERLOADED
#   accessor set -- PickAccessor keeps the candidates whose arity range
#   contains the property's index count (+1 for a setter, read off the
#   declaring line by PropertyIndexArity) and answers only a unique survivor;
#   same-count overloads decline (accessor 0, no call edge) and a declined set
#   on the declaring class stops the ancestor walk. FindSymbolsByExactName is
#   a READER and is not in the manifest. Remedy when an index exists:
#   index --all --resolve-only.
#
#   Superseded: 1.4.0-alpha|a35513046797f2f0cf416752672496d55bec00368bb9e08238e0279eb4004389

