# 2026-09-19: manifest WIDENED (FindSymbolsByExactName / FoldStubs / the
#   DRagLint.Core.ForwardStub unit added as resolve surface after the C2.5
#   review); code on the previously-listed surface unchanged. WHY THEY ARE
#   SURFACE: DRagLint.Index.CallResolver.pas:2176 calls FindSymbolsByExactName
#   on the extra stores for a receiver's type and declines on Found <> 1, so
#   what that reader returns decides which call_edges are written -- the
#   manifest's own closure rule. The hash moves only because the manifest grew
#   (three new hashed spans); every span that was already listed hashes to what
#   it did before. The C2.5 behaviour change itself (RTL forward stubs such as
#   TComponent/TReader/TWriter were 2 rows and are now 1, so cross-store
#   receivers that used to decline now resolve) is recorded in CHANGELOG
#   Unreleased and awaits the owner's bump decision; until then an index
#   resolved before C2.5 lacks those edges (remedy when the owner bumps:
#   index --all --resolve-only). Found by the review, not by the drift regex.
#
#   Superseded: 1.4.0-alpha|cc8c86896c828038e9eeb9102faa988fe9aede73f4c6aa0eef65b7049322c2e0

# 2026-09-21: 1.4.0-alpha -> 1.5.0-alpha (purity v2, plan C6.1). A new `purity`
#   resolve stage -- src\analysis\DRagLint.Analysis.PurityStage.pas over the
#   pure model in src\analysis\DRagLint.Analysis.Purity.pas -- derives
#   symbol_facts.effect_free / effect_summary / effect_witness from call_edges,
#   member_accesses, refs and routine bodies the index already holds. DERIVED
#   columns only, no parse change: remedy is index --all --resolve-only.
#
#   THE MANIFEST WAS WIDENED, AND A LITERAL READING OF THE HEADER ABOVE WOULD
#   HAVE REFUSED IT. That header scopes the resolve surface to "the code that
#   DERIVES call_edges, type_ancestors, type_helpers and unit_uses targets", and
#   the purity stage derives none of those -- it writes symbol_facts columns.
#   Both analysis units go in anyway, and the reason is the staleness mechanics
#   rather than the list of tables:
#
#     TPurityStage recomputes ONLY when PurityNeedsRun is True, i.e. only while
#     some row with body_loc > 0 still has effect_free IS NULL. Once a database
#     has been FILLED by a stage, every row has a verdict, PurityNeedsRun goes
#     False, and that database keeps the OLD verdicts forever. There is no
#     second trigger -- not a changed file, not a re-lint, not a re-resolve of
#     the call pass. The resolver fingerprint is the ONLY thing left that can
#     force it to think again.
#
#   So without these entries, any future change to purity logic goes silently
#   stale in every index: the columns are populated, the answers look complete,
#   and they are the previous build's. That is verbatim the failure mode this
#   file's own header calls out -- "the failure mode of getting it wrong is
#   SILENT" -- and it is why the entry is judged by what the stamp PROTECTS
#   rather than by which four tables the header happens to name.
#
#   THIS IS THE SAME PRINCIPLE AS THE 2026-09-19 WIDENING, ONE STEP FURTHER.
#   That entry admitted a READER the resolve pass depends on (FindSymbolsByExactName
#   / FoldStubs), on the manifest's own closure rule: a routine that decides
#   what is WRITTEN is surface even though it writes nothing. This entry extends
#   the same rule from readers the pass depends on to WRITES the pass performs
#   -- a second derived-data producer, sharing the one resolve stamp because it
#   shares the one remedy and the one silent-staleness hazard.
#
#   WHAT ELSE MOVED THE HASH, so the diff is not mistaken for code drift:
#   the manifest gained the two analysis units (hashed whole, `::*`) plus the
#   store surface the stage uses -- PutEffectFacts, PurityNeedsRun,
#   GetAllSymbolFacts, FindSymbolsWithFacts, DumpAllMemberAccesses -- and
#   DumpAllCallEdges MOVED OUT OF THE EXCLUSION LIST. It had been excluded as a
#   query-side reader on the stated ground that "a reader cannot make stored
#   data stale"; PurityStage.pas:578 now loads every call edge through it, one
#   line above the DumpAllMemberAccesses call, so that ground is false and the
#   exclusion's reason no longer held. Every span that was already listed hashes
#   to what it hashed before; no previously-listed code changed in this commit.
#
#   KNOWN AND DELIBERATE GAP, recorded in the manifest beside the entries: the
#   stage reads eight further store routines (FindAllChildSymbols,
#   FindChildSymbolByName, FindSymbolsByKind, GetAllFileStamps, GetFilePath,
#   GetReferencesFromFile, GetSymbolById, and GetTransitiveAncestors which was
#   already listed). Strict closure puts all of them in; widening that far is a
#   scoping decision larger than this stage and is left for the owner. It is
#   written down rather than skipped so that a purity verdict changing without
#   this guard noticing is diagnosable instead of mysterious.
#
#   THE C2.5 CROSS-STORE QUESTION RECORDED IN THE 2026-09-19 ENTRY IS NOT
#   SETTLED HERE. That bump still awaits the owner's decision; this bump is
#   about purity and carries no verdict on it. An index re-resolved under
#   1.5.0-alpha does, as a side effect, pick the C2.5 edges up -- worth knowing,
#   but not a decision this entry is making.
#
#   Superseded: 1.4.0-alpha|463989bb0a729a967964a9a29ec5913d23133ed5eb6d1d5611b3a89c1acee2d3

# 2026-09-22 (Task 6, T4-R3 correction; controller ruling T6-R2): hash re-pinned
